@@ -75,6 +75,15 @@ parsed. *Extra whitespace is ignored*::
     >>> parse_string('  control_change   control=1  value=122')
     Message('control_change', channel=0, control=1, value=122, time=0)
 
+SysEx data is a comma-separated sequence of decimal bytes. Parentheses
+are included when encoding a message but are optional when parsing::
+
+    >>> parse_string('sysex data=10,20,30')
+    Message('sysex', data=(10, 20, 30), time=0)
+
+Use ``data=()`` for an empty data sequence. Spaces are not allowed within
+the data sequence.
+
 To parse messages from a stream, you can use
 ``mido.messages.parse_string_stream()``::
 
